---
import BaseLayout from '@/layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import PageHeader from '@/components/PageHeader.astro';
import { SITE } from '@/data/site';
import { url } from '@/lib/url';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="About ind-ds"
  description="Why ind-ds exists: industrial software teams rebuild the same alarms, states, faceplates and controls project after project. ind-ds is an open, reusable foundation."
>
  <PageHeader
    eyebrow="About"
    title="About the project"
    lead="ind-ds was created from a recurring observation: industrial software teams rebuild the same states, alarms, equipment indicators, controls and layout conventions project after project — often without a shared vocabulary or reusable implementation."
    crumbs={[{ label: 'Home', href: url('/') }, { label: 'About' }]}
  />

  <section class="section"><div class="container about">
    <div class="about__prose stack-lg">
      <div>
        <h2>The problem</h2>
        <p>
          Web technology now powers a large share of HMI, SCADA, monitoring and control interfaces —
          in browsers, embedded panels, Electron and Tauri shells and WebViews. Yet most teams build
          those interfaces on generic UI kits designed for marketing sites and back-office SaaS.
        </p>
        <p>
          Those kits offer buttons, forms, cards and tables, but nothing that understands a pump’s
          operating state, an ISA-18.2 alarm priority, an acknowledgement, a setpoint or a
          connection status. So every project re-implements LEDs, valves, alarm tables, trends,
          machine states and control layouts by hand — inconsistently, and rarely with a shared
          design language between applications.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>The goal</h2>
        <p>
          ind-ds aims to provide that missing industrial layer as an open, reusable foundation:
          framework-agnostic Web Components with real process semantics, typed React and Vue
          wrappers, cross-platform design tokens and helpers for binding live data. The visual
          language and semantic contracts stay consistent across applications and technologies, and
          teams can adopt only the parts they need.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Open-source philosophy</h2>
        <p>
          The project is MIT licensed and developed in the open. It is intentionally unopinionated
          about your HMI philosophy: it gives you consistent building blocks and a shared vocabulary,
          and supports teams implementing their own design standards rather than prescribing one.
          Real industrial feedback — from developers, controls engineers and designers — shapes what
          gets built.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2>Maintainer</h2>
        <p>
          ind-ds was created by <strong>{SITE.author.name}</strong>, a software architect and
          frontend specialist with experience in industrial software and HMI-related projects. It is
          an independent open-source project, not affiliated with or certified by ISA, ANSI, IEC or
          the W3C.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <aside class="about__side">
      <div class="panel about__card">
        <h2>Explore</h2>
        <ul class="about__links">
          <li><a href={url('/components')}>All {SITE.componentCount} components</a></li>
          <li><a href={url('/principles')}>Design principles</a></li>
          <li><a href={url('/roadmap')}>Roadmap</a></li>
          <li><a href={url('/contributing')}>Contributing</a></li>
        </ul>
        <h2 class="about__h2">Links</h2>
        <ul class="about__links">
          <li><a href={SITE.repo} target="_blank" rel="noopener">GitHub repository</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.storybook} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Storybook</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.npmOrg} target="_blank" rel="noopener">npm packages</a></li>
          <li><a href={SITE.author.github} target="_blank" rel="noopener">Maintainer on GitHub</a></li>
        </ul>
      </div>
    </aside>
  </div></section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .about { display: grid; grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) 16rem; gap: var(--ind-spacing-8); align-items: start; }
  .about__prose h2 { margin-top: 0; }
  .about__prose p { max-width: 66ch; }
  .about__card { padding: var(--ind-spacing-5); position: sticky; top: calc(var(--site-header-h) + var(--ind-spacing-4)); }
  .about__card h2 { font-size: var(--ind-font-size-md); margin: 0 0 var(--ind-spacing-3); }
  .about__h2 { margin-top: var(--ind-spacing-5) !important; }
  .about__links { list-style: none; margin: 0; padding: 0; display: grid; gap: var(--ind-spacing-2); }
  .about__links a { font-size: var(--ind-font-size-sm); color: var(--ind-surface-text-secondary); text-decoration: none; }
  .about__links a:hover { color: var(--ind-surface-text-primary); text-decoration: underline; }
  @media (max-width: 820px) { .about { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } .about__card { position: static; } }
</style>
